"""
Nova Light Curve UI (Tkinter)
--------------------------------
A single-file Python app that replicates your current light-curve plotting script
(t_peak at JD=tpeak_JD, m_peak horizontal, t2 at JD=t2_JD, shaded asymmetric
uncertainty regions using both quadrature and bracket-between-observations logic)
— but with a GUI to:

• Open one or many data files and quickly switch between them
• Autodetect columns (JD/HJD, Mag/Magnitude, MagErr/Uncertainty, Band/Filter)
• Manually remap columns via dropdowns if autodetect guesses wrong
• Optionally filter by Band/Filter (if present)
• Choose and apply a sentinel “bad magnitude” value (default 99.999)
• Enter t_peak JD, m_peak, t2 JD, and optional manual_tpeak_before override
• Plot with Matplotlib embedded in Tkinter + print the uncertainty readout
• Save the current plot as PNG

Supported file types / formats (auto-parsed):
• .csv (any delimiter — auto-sniffed)
• .txt / .dat with whitespace or mixed delimiters; comment lines (#, !, ;) ignored
• AAVSO-style CSVs with headers like JD/HJD, Magnitude, Uncertainty, Band, etc.
  (non-numeric mags such as "<14.2" are treated as upper limits and dropped by default)

Requires: Python 3.8+, matplotlib, pandas, numpy
  pip install matplotlib pandas numpy

Author: You (starting from your existing analysis logic)
"""

